description: Keep Python dataclasses limited to DTO-style data containers
globs: "**/*.py"
alwaysApply: true
---

# Dataclass Usage Policy

- In this project, `@dataclass` is used only for DTO-style containers (named fields, defaults, and structured data transfer).
- Dataclasses may validate their own field invariants in `__post_init__`.
- Dataclasses may include computed `@property` accessors derived from their own fields.
- Business logic, service behavior, IO, and network calls must be implemented in regular classes or functions, not dataclasses.
